course: dictionary
lesson: 11672
title: Assigned: given to someone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Assigned means given to someone as a job, a task or a place. When a teacher gives you a job, it is assigned to you. «The homework assigned by the teacher was ten maths sums.» The sums were given out as a task, so assigned means given.
explain: Assigned can also mean put in a certain place or group. «Your assigned seat is at the back, next to Mia.» The teacher has chosen where you sit, so the seat has been picked for you. Look at the words around assigned to find out which meaning fits.
explain: In maths, assigned means that a value is given to a letter. «In the sum, x is assigned the value 7.» That means x stands for the number 7. Context is the key: the words near assigned tell you which meaning it has.
fact: Assigned is the past form of the verb assign.
fact: Assign, assigns, assigned and assigning are all forms of the same verb.
fact: «Assigned reading» means reading that a teacher has given you to do.
fact: «Be assigned to» means be given to a person, group or place: «Ravi was assigned to the blue group.»
fact: In maths and computing, assigning a value to a variable, like x = 5, means giving the letter that value.
exercise: «The homework assigned by the teacher was ten maths sums.» What does assigned mean here? | Finished early | *Given as a task | Hidden under a desk | Lost on the way home
exercise: «Your assigned seat is at the back, next to Mia.» What does assigned mean here? | Broken | Painted bright blue | *Put in a certain place | Made of wood
exercise: In the sum, «x is assigned the value 7», what does x stand for? | *The number 7 | The teacher's name | The word seven | A colour
test: Which word is the past form of assign? | assigning | assigns | *assigned | assign
test: «Ravi was assigned to the blue group.» Which phrase means nearly the same as was assigned to? | was tired of | was lost in | was afraid of | *was put in
exam: «Each pupil was assigned a partner for the science project.» What does assigned mean? | *Given to someone as a task or group | Lost | Sold | Forgotten
